// CyberCut / TwoPremium / Special / SevenThreePremium / SevenThreeNeumorphism /
// TwoNeumorphism / 3Three for FloatingBadge / 3ThreeCyberCut / Neumorphism /
// SevenThreeCyberCut / SevenThree (base) / ContentBox (base) / TwoFloatingBadge —
// **zero file overlap with the outgoing brand's mix.** NavbarStyle4 + FooterPremiumSumo
// are the layout's pair this round and the brand font moves kanit -> google-sans; all
// of that is the orchestrator's shared-chrome step, not this page's.
// ⚠️ ContentBox.astro (the base) IS in this round's mix — it carries docx §6 — and it
// is also always-live shared chrome, because terms, privacy, 404, /promotion, /ทางเข้า
// and the button pages all render through it. The orchestrator owns and rethemes that
// file; **this page imports and uses it but never edits it.** An "is it used?" check
// has to match the bare filename rather than the components/ path, which is how a
// component reached only from another file got misread as inventory once.
// Every unused *Style / *Premium / *Cyber / *Huay / *CyberCut / *FloatingBadge sibling,
// the other Faq* and Announcement* files, the other LatestWinners* and ReviewCardSumo2
// all stay on disk as inventory for the next brand — nothing was deleted, and the
// earlier brands' hues still inside them are expected drift.
//
// Nine widgets this template usually offers are deliberately absent, and they are named
// without their file extension on purpose because the playbook's "is this component
// live?" check is a bare-filename grep: ProviderGrid and ProviderGridPremium are out
// because this brief names NO game studio at all — it says "ค่ายตรงมาแรง" and
// "ค่ายต่าง ๆ" and never one name — BankStrip is out for the same reason on the banking
// side, since the brief names no bank and no wallet, GameRankingBoard has no ranking to
// carry, SmoothCarousel has no brief section asking for a carousel, LoginRtpSection is
// out because its RTP table would put an RTP figure on the page while §6 allows only
// the brief's own numbers (0.3%, 0.8%, 24ชม., ปี 2026), and FeaturedGames /
// PopularGamesStrip / LottoGrid would all have to invent game or market names the brief
// never writes.
// ⚠️ FeatureHighlights IS used this round, unlike the last two: the brief gives docx §6
// a real three-item sub-list (ขั้นตอนที่ 1 / 2 / 3, content.txt lines 15-20), which is
// exactly the one sanctioned shape for H3s under an H2.
//
// <Announcement /> runs bare on purpose: AnnouncementPremium's default message is this
// brand's copy, written from this brief by the orchestrator, and every sub-page calls it
// bare too — so passing an override here is exactly how the ticker ends up saying two
// different things on two pages of the same site.
//
// PALETTE — CHERRY RED LEADING, BURNT COPPER SECOND, RED-BROWN INK ON **LIGHT SURFACES**
// (brand-spec §2). ⚠️⚠️ **THIS IS THE FOURTH LIGHT-THEME BRAND IN THIS REPO** and the
// third in a row, so the direction is not the novelty — the HUE is. bg.json for this
// drop is {"mode":"color","color":"#ffd1d1"}, a pastel pink page background, and bg.json
// is the ONLY source of that value: do not inherit a dark page from any earlier round
// and do not "fix" it back to black. Every ContentBox*, FeatureHighlights, the FAQ and
// the review ledger therefore run LIGHT surfaces (#ffffff raised / #fff4ea inset) with
